{"number":6,"title":"Cubes & Cube Roots","slug":"cubes-and-cube-roots","color":"","level":"","estTime":"","description":"Class 8 IMO — Cubes & cube roots: perfect cubes, finding cubes by prime factorisation, cube roots by the prime factorisation method, and volume word problems.","topics":[{"title":"Perfect Cubes","concept":"<p>A <strong>perfect cube</strong> is a number that is the cube of a whole number. The first few are 1, 8, 27, 64, 125, 216, 343, 512, 729 and 1000. The cube of a number n is n × n × n.</p>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"What is 4³?","solution":"4 × 4 × 4 = 64."},{"number":"2","problem":"What is 5³?","solution":"5 × 5 × 5 = 125."}],"recap":["A perfect cube = the cube of a whole number.","Cubes: 1, 8, 27, 64, 125, 216, 343, 512, 729, 1000."],"quiz":[{"q":"What is 3³?","options":["9","18","27","81"],"correct":2,"explanation":"3 × 3 × 3 = 27.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Which of these is a perfect cube?","options":["16","27","50","100"],"correct":1,"explanation":"27 = 3³.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"}]},{"title":"Finding Cubes by Prime Factorisation","concept":"<p>To check whether a number is a perfect cube, write its <strong>prime factorisation</strong> and group the primes in threes. If every prime forms complete groups of three, the number is a perfect cube.</p>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"What is 6³?","solution":"6 × 6 × 6 = 216."},{"number":"2","problem":"What is 10³?","solution":"10 × 10 × 10 = 1000."}],"recap":["Group prime factors in threes to test for a perfect cube.","n³ = n × n × n."],"quiz":[{"q":"What is 7³?","options":["243","294","343","392"],"correct":2,"explanation":"7 × 7 × 7 = 343.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is 8³?","options":["256","512","488","576"],"correct":1,"explanation":"8 × 8 × 8 = 512.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]},{"title":"Cube Roots & Volume Problems","concept":"<p>The <strong>cube root</strong> reverses cubing: the cube root of 125 is 5 because 5³ = 125. The volume of a cube of side a is a³, so a cube of side 4 has volume 64.</p>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"What is the cube root of 125?","solution":"5, since 5³ = 125."},{"number":"2","problem":"A cube has side 4 cm. What is its volume?","solution":"4³ = 64 cm³."}],"recap":["Cube root reverses cubing (∛125 = 5).","Volume of a cube = side³."],"quiz":[{"q":"What is the cube root of 216?","options":["4","5","6","8"],"correct":2,"explanation":"6³ = 216.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is the cube root of 343?","options":["6","7","8","9"],"correct":1,"explanation":"7³ = 343.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]}],"tests":{"online":{"title":"","minutes":18,"questions":[{"q":"1, 8, 27, 64 are cubes. What comes next?","options":["100","121","125","144"],"correct":2,"explanation":"5³ = 125.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Which of these is a perfect cube?","options":["36","49","64","100"],"correct":2,"explanation":"64 = 4³.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"What is the cube root of 1?","options":["0","1","2","3"],"correct":1,"explanation":"1³ = 1.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"What is the cube of 2?","options":["4","6","8","16"],"correct":2,"explanation":"2 × 2 × 2 = 8.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"What is 4³?","options":["12","16","48","64"],"correct":3,"explanation":"4 × 4 × 4 = 64.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"What is 5³?","options":["75","100","125","150"],"correct":2,"explanation":"5 × 5 × 5 = 125.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"What is the cube root of 125?","options":["4","5","6","25"],"correct":1,"explanation":"5³ = 125.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is the cube root of 216?","options":["5","6","7","8"],"correct":1,"explanation":"6³ = 216.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is 6³?","options":["196","206","216","226"],"correct":2,"explanation":"6 × 6 × 6 = 216.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is the cube root of 729?","options":["7","8","9","11"],"correct":2,"explanation":"9³ = 729.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A cubic box has side 5 cm. What is its volume?","options":["75 cm³","100 cm³","125 cm³","150 cm³"],"correct":2,"explanation":"5³ = 125 cm³.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A cube has volume 64 cm³. What is its side?","options":["2 cm","3 cm","4 cm","8 cm"],"correct":2,"explanation":"∛64 = 4 cm.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is the cube root of 1000?","options":["10","20","100","30"],"correct":0,"explanation":"10³ = 1000.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"A cube has volume 343 cm³. What is the total length of all 12 edges?","options":["49 cm","72 cm","84 cm","96 cm"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Side = ∛343 = 7 cm, so 12 × 7 = 84 cm.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"}]}}}